      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14193183/assets/671faf1efc8d64c4db563140d6d9bc8e080c1591eef92d44a5d7f381be115c95.png)\n\nFind the measure of angle $B.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since the sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is ${180}^{∘}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{27}^{∘}+3x+(5x+{9}^{∘}) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {36}^{∘}+8x & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ 8x & ={144}^{∘} \\\\ x & ={18}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nm∠B=5x+{9}^{∘}=5({18}^{∘})+{9}^{∘}={99}^{∘}.\n$$",
